WEBVTT

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:05.480
So you wanna be a train driver, huh, Takayama?

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.230
Huh?

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.980
Oh, yeah.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.230
I think that's a good idea.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.610
If you're driving, I might
even take a ride one day.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:18.360
I can understand where
they're coming from, though.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:25.160
It's like going to an event all dressed up
only to find out the spotlight wasn't on me.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.210
Wh-What?

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.340
It's really embarrassing.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.630
Makes you wanna take it out on others.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.720
Wh-What does that have
to do with anything?

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.430
You've totally got the wrong idea.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.350
Oh? Who's got the wrong idea, now?

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:46.060
Well, not that I mind this situation.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.770
What?

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:53.060
O-Oh, nothing.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:56.320
I'm free to have feelings for
whomever I want, right?

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.490
H-Hey, Noa!

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.360
Can't take a little attention?

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.910
Attention? This isn't really the timeвЂ”

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.200
Are you feeling shy?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.580
W-Well...

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:09.500
Oh!

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.790
There you are, Takayama!

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:13.040
Here.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.130
It's really pouring out there.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.590
Thanks, Sasshou.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.380
Want some, Noa?

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.180
Go ahead.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.350
Wait, don't you remember?

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:32.850
I texted her to buy us something warm.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.440
You're quite a playboy, Takayama.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:37.230
Huh?

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.820
Whatever.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.570
I can fight for my man if I have to.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:42.610
Here.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:44.160
Thanks.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:44.910
Thank you so much.

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:46.780
Well, I gotta go.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:47.290
Huh?

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.910
I've got a rehearsal soon.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.750
It was Sasshou, right? Thanks for the drink.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.130
You're welcome.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.420
This is Takayama.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.460
Instructor Narita?

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:00.800
Now?

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.130
We're in town.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.640
Right.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.430
What?!

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.310
Understood.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.510
We'll be right there.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.640
There was a rockslide in Kumanotaira!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.150
The Shinshu Express is stuck in Yagasaki.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.780
We're to go there and help
guide the passengers out.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.990
Sorry, but we've got to go!

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.870
Right. Good luck.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.200
I wouldn't mind seeing you
in a driver's uniform...

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.210
but you do look pretty cool
when you're saluting.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.710
We're sorry for the inconvenience!

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:46.720
Karuizawa Station is currently
taken up by the following train.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.680
You'll have to walk from here.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.390
We ask for your assistance at this time.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.060
Don't panic!

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.520
Watch where you're going and proceed calmly!

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.490
Looks like you're all washed up.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.740
But you really saved us.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.370
Good work.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.080
I made the coffee, so it'll probably taste bad.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.420
It'll at least warm you up after being in the rain, though.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.250
Thank you very much.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:19.840
Here.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:21.210
ThвЂ”

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.670
Thank you.

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:26.680
Sakurai.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.220
Your coffee'll go cold.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:30.720
I know.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:33.770
Yech.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.140
You have to start the trains up again!

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.900
I'm sorry, but we can't.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:40.360
I'm begging you, here!

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:42.360
What's up?

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.190
Well, this ladyвЂ”

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.400
I really need to take a train!

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.950
It's just not possible right now.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:53.160
Including the full inspection, clearing the track will take at least four hours.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.250
I need to deliver this!

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.750
Someone's life hangs in the balance!

00:06:00.590 --> 00:06:03.750
How about we let her explain?

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.420
S-Sir!

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:07.760
You were here, sir?

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.590
Were you all right in all this rain?

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.010
Who's that?

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:10.430
Dunno.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:11.390
We're so far out.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.430
Someone high up in the PSF, judging from their reactions.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.560
Never mind me.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.720
Someone high up in the PSF, judging from their reactions.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:18.730
My name is Oito, and I work for the Japanese Organs Transit System.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:26.320
I was in the middle of driving organs destined for transplants when the roads got closed down.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:31.780
I got this far by taking a train, but now I'm stuck.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.160
I'm afraid the rails are the same as the roads.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:40.500
Service on both the Shinetsu Main Line and Hokuriku Bullet Train is suspended due to the rockslide.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.460
What about the Hokuriku Expressway?

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:44.630
It'd be a detour, but...

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.210
The organs would never last!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:51.340
I've got to deliver them to a hospital
in Maebashi within two hours!

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:56.850
But with the rails, roads,
and other services closed...

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.480
Please.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:01.350
I'll do it!

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.980
If we can't take a train, then someone has to run the rest of the way!

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:10.400
We can still make it to Yokokawa in two hours if we leave now!

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.860
Calm down, Haruka.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:16.370
There's no way to guarantee we'll
make it to Yokokawa in two hours.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.960
And even if we could, Maebashi would still be too far away!

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.620
Well, we have to try!

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.590
A transplant can save someone's life!

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:31.630
Whoever donated the organs must have
passed away believing they could still do good.

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:32.970
Haruka.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:38.180
I'm not going to give up on that hope just because of a little rain!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.310
Hold on, Koumi.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.520
What? We're running out of time!

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:47.150
There might be a way to make it to
Yokokawa even quicker, if we're lucky.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.360
Huh?

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.740
The rockslide was ahead of Kumanotaira.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:53.410
So the old line should still be okay, right?

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:58.660
Probably. It hasn't been maintained much, though, so who knows what it's like.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.960
But it's not impossible to take.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:07.630
Yes. We didn't find any broken sections during our inspection in the spring.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.130
Good. Then let's take the old line!

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.260
It should help us move a little quicker.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.510
I'll come with you.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.100
Takayama!

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.060
No way you'll make it.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.930
What? It's just hiking down a mountain.

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.730
Marching in the rain really tests your stamina.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.980
You're gonna need me, too.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:33.450
And with four people, your chances of
delivering the goods to Yokokawa are higher.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:36.780
Guys!

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.370
This year's K4 certainly is an interesting bunch.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.540
Huh?

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:43.750
Wakayama.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.620
Y-Yes, sir?

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.210
Can't we give them a draisine?

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.470
An ED42?

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.140
Kinda small, though.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:00.680
This is the EB42 draisine, nicknamed Abtty.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:04.190
Is this amusement park ride really gonna help?

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.480
And why "Abtty"?

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.900
What's this?

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:14.030
This draisine was designed to be pedaled by four people.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.490
It only has one working set of pedals right now, though.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:21.950
It's equipped with a battery, and two front and rear wheels are assisted by an electric motor.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.660
You should be able to make it downhill.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:30.380
In the rear of the car is the resistor for dynamic braking, Unit D.

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:35.840
It'll be your lifeline while descending through the Usui Pass, so make careful use of it.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.840
This is the operations manual.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.800
Whoa!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.100
Leave it to me!

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:43.720
Wow.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.480
Let her handle that. Just hurry!

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.180
Thank you so much.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.730
My colleague is waiting at Yokokawa Station. You can hand it to them there.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:29.810
All right. Leave it to us.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:31.230
Quit your whining!

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.900
These are my pupils heading out there.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.650
Do as you're told!

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:36.990
Takayama!

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:40.450
I've relayed what you kids are planning to the people further down the line.

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.660
You can ignore any signals!

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.160
Y-Yes, sir!

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.660
Done reading!

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:46.750
Okay!

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.410
Let's do this!

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.120
We'll leave the driving to you.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:50.830
Huh?

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:54.630
Who else can do it but you?

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:57.550
Yeah, Mr. Future Driver.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.630
Y-Yeah.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:02.890
Then give us our orders, Deputy.

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.390
Whatcha want from me, Deputy?

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.020
Awaiting orders, Deputy!

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:11.020
All right!

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:13.110
I'll drive!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:16.280
Koumi, you help everyone work the car.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:19.190
Iwaizumi, you pedal and power the car.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.240
Sakurai, be on standby for emergencies.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:24.830
Roger!

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.410
We're off!

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.500
Thank you.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.080
Just a minute!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:36.920
We haven't used this car in so long the battery must be dead!

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:43.140
According to the manual, the electric motor isn't just to assist. It's also integrated into the battery.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:48.270
Pedaling to turn the engine
should charge the battery.

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.140
Got it!

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.780
Heavy bastard!

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:04.530
It's impossible! This car is too big for one person to start.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.910
It'd be quicker to go back and change the battery!

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:10.040
Sakurai!

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:12.620
We don't have time for that.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:18.550
I guess me and these clothes just weren't meant to be.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.220
Now I have a full range of motion.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:33.890
Forcing the wheels to turn will give us electricity, right?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.860
It's just like pushing a bike before pedaling.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.360
Iwaizumi!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.070
Give it your all!

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.320
Yeah!

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.780
I'll pedal so hard I rip the wheels right off!

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:47.370
I-I'll helpвЂ”

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.490
You focus on driving.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:54.750
That's right. Focus on what only
you can do, and give it your best.

00:12:55.750 --> 00:12:56.250
Right!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:59.750
On three, now! All together!

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:02.420
Deputy, start us off!

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.640
L-Let's go!

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.100
One!

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:09.850
Two!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:11.270
Three!

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.870
Voltage rising!

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.240
We can do this!

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.250
You get on too, Sakurai.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:42.960
B-But...

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:44.630
We can handle the rest.

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.130
Go on ahead.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.550
Sakurai!

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:51.810
Sorry.

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:52.810
Goodbye!

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:07.240
Don't let us down, K4!

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.820
Thank you very much!

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.330
After the descent you're almost there!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.120
Good luck!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.570
Takayama?

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:51.990
Running a red light is something
you're never supposed to do as a driver.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:13.930
We're starting the descent.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:15.310
All right.

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:25.730
Iwaizumi!

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:27.690
Stop pedaling!

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.530
What'd you say?

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:31.910
Stop pedaling!

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:32.660
What?

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.330
It's too dangerous to go any faster!

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.490
Roger!

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:43.080
Pulling the driver side lever will brake just the rear two wheels.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.080
Okay!

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:02.640
We're not slowing down!

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:04.900
This is like a roller coaster!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:09.030
We're in tunnel #9, the longest in Usui Pass.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:11.280
How many tunnels are there?

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:12.780
Sixteen more.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:19.450
The new tunnels leading up to the halfway point, Kumanotaira Signal Station, are nice and big,

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:23.250
but beyond that the tunnels
date back as far as the Meiji Period.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:24.540
We have to be careful.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.850
I'm sorry, Takayama.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.890
It-It's okay.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.230
Takayama, we're tilting!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:52.240
Crap, we're gonna roll!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:56.070
Iwaizumi, can you get us centered again?

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:58.200
Roger that, Deputy!

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:04.410
Th-Thanks.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:09.500
We have to slow down,
or things will get sticky real fast.

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:12.590
Aoi, activate the Unit D resistors!

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.510
You mean this thing with "D" written on it?

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.590
Yeah. Pull it!

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.140
It's a dynamic braking system.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:28.650
Damn.

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.400
We're not slowing!

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:35.490
The Unit D takes a little time to take effect.

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:38.870
This one's bigger!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.830
We're not gonna make the turn!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:41.870
Aoi?!

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.210
Honestly, never a dull day
with you, huh, Takayama?

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:47.210
Wh-What are you doing?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.670
It's way too dangerous to stand there!

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.960
It's dangerous everywhere!

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:05.060
Damn you!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.450
Two butts are better than one, right?

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.740
Sure are!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:33.920
We have to slow down more before we hit the old track.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:38.380
But will the brake last that long?

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.470
Aoi, Iwaizumi!

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:43.350
There's an S-curve coming up!

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:46.060
We're going left then right!

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:46.980
Roger!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.190
Here we go!

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.570
Right coming up!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.670
One more time!

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:26.180
Nice!

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:28.770
And what was with the screaming?

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.560
You sounded like an idiot.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:34.690
Well, maybe I <i>am</i> an idiot.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:35.860
Huh?

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.900
What a stupid rivalry.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.780
And over a train nerd, of all people.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:42.070
Ow!

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:45.080
Yeah. We're just dumb.

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:48.120
Ow, hot!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:51.420
Is this thing malfunctioning?

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:57.170
No, that actually indicates the Unit D
dynamic braking is working fine.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.550
Are you sure this isn't too hot?

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:04.050
The electricity generated is turned into heat with the resistors and consumed.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:07.350
According to the manual,
it <i>is</i> supposed to get a little hot.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:21.110
Here we are.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.030
Kumanotaira.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:35.880
Good work!

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:46.300
There's no telling how the old track is holding up, so be careful!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.930
Thanks, fellas!

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.600
Thank you!

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:53.810
We'll do our best!

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.730
Thank you.

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.570
We're hitting the old track.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:08.990
The shaking might get stronger.

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:13.080
Koumi, hold that container tight.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:13.830
Right!

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:16.000
How many tunnels are left?

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:19.250
Ten, and then we'll be in Yokokawa.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:23.340
So basically we've cleared half of them, right?

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:24.840
It's only gonna get tougher.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:30.350
This line isn't normally used.
In this rain, who knows what'll happen?

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:34.480
Falling rocks could take us out instantly.

00:21:39.440 --> 00:21:42.150
But we can't let that stop us, right?

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:43.780
We're together all the way!

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:45.650
We <i>will</i> deliver these organs!

00:21:45.650 --> 00:21:48.160
Once more unto the breach, dear friends!

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.330
Thanks, guys.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:54.960
Takayama!

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:45.610
The 11.2 kilometers between Yokokawa and Karuizawa have been dubbed the Abt Area,

00:23:45.610 --> 00:23:48.860
with a steep slope running up to 66.7 permille.

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:51.450
The toothed rack rail interlocking

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:55.450
with the gear beneath a train car engine combine to form the Abt system.

00:23:55.450 --> 00:23:57.830
The shining, black rails!
The clacking of the gears!

00:23:57.830 --> 00:23:58.870
Howl!

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:00.370
Special Move: Me Brakes!

00:24:00.710 --> 00:24:03.290
Rail Wars, Episode Nine: Thank You.

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:05.670
Huh? Abtty won't slow down?

00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:06.670
Roger that!

00:24:06.670 --> 00:24:07.960
Leave it to me!
